= January 2023 — A key that may not turn

Prime Minister Mateusz Morawiecki's government has sent the Sejm another repair
to the judicial disciplinary system. This time it would move judges' cases to the Supreme
Administrative Court, and PiS presents every clause as a key to Poland's frozen
recovery fund.

The European Commission still has to decide whether the law meets its
milestones. President **[+ president_name +]** can still send the text to the
Constitutional Tribunal. Lewica is being asked to lend its votes before either
institution has promised that a single euro will move.

- @jan23_verify
- @jan23_unlock
- @jan23_palace
- @jan23_oppose

@jan23_verify
title: Support only independently verified milestones
on-arrival: kpo_bill_quality = 3; judicial_legitimacy += 4; constitutional_restraint += 3; ko_relation += 2; pis_relation -= 2; news_headline = "The Left makes verification the price of support"

Lewica's lawyers publish their test clause by clause and refuse to let the vote
outrun it. Brussels now has a Polish opposition party demanding verification,
not merely another declaration from Morawiecki. The money remains frozen for
the moment, but so does PiS's attempt to make us certify its workmanship.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue


@jan23_unlock
title: Accept an imperfect law to unlock investment
on-arrival: kpo_bill_quality = 2; kpo_scrutiny += 4; household_policy_pressure += 2; institutional_trust -= 3; public_trust -= 1; pis_relation += 3; ko_relation -= 3; razem_dissent += 5; last_policy_stage = "Negotiated concession"; last_policy_authority = "PiS cabinet and parliamentary majority"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Recovery investment outranks another perfect court bill"

Our votes give Morawiecki the law he wanted. Mayors and hospital directors can
at last plan around the prospect of recovery money; there is still no automatic
payment, only a better chance of one. Razem and KO spend the evening asking why
Lewica trusted the same government that broke the courts in the first place.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue


@jan23_palace
title: Negotiate the text with the president before the vote
on-arrival: kpo_bill_quality = 2; president_relation += 5; presidential_channel_open = 1; constitutional_restraint += 2; ko_relation -= 1; news_headline = "The Palace is asked to own the KPO exit"

The bill moves from the committee room to the Presidential Palace before the
Sejm has settled it. President **[+ president_name +]** gains the right to call
the compromise his own—and the room to bury it. Lewica has opened a channel,
but it has also made the president the gatekeeper of Poland's recovery money.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue


@jan23_oppose
title: Reject the bill as another relabelling
on-arrival: kpo_bill_quality = 0; judicial_legitimacy += 2; kpo_delivery -= 2; pis_relation -= 4; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "The Left refuses another renamed disciplinary system"

Lewica will not put a European seal on a disciplinary system with a new name.
Judges' associations welcome the refusal; municipalities waiting for investment
hear only that the delay continues. PiS knows which half of that sentence it
wants repeated on the evening news.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue
